{"explanation": "The unit's strongest drive is at the class level: dogs and other canids (dingo, corgis, foxes, wolves, hounds), plus a few other animals and balls. Within those classes, none of the annotated photo properties reliably explains its activity. The apparent preference for left-facing subjects over right-facing ones (rows 1, 2 and 5) and for warm-tinted photos (row 13) did not replicate on 109 new photos. All four rows fell to unremarkable or even reversed effects (percentiles 13 to 65). Framing, subject size, cut-off, position, lighting, tilt and sharpness effects were never unusual for this layer (all below 95). No row can be confidently said to describe something particular to this unit.", "rows": []}
```

